   "text": "cryptoAGI/voaice — What a voice is, written down: .voaice identities for NEURAL and JAIMLA, an 18-decimal voiceprint that Python and the browser agree on, and vCLONE microphone capture. Measures; does not clone. What a voice is, written down — and a way to check that a recording came from it. A .voaice is not audio and it is not a model. It is an identity card: which model speaks the voice, what it measured as, and a vprint over those measurements — eight acoustic metrics in 18-decimal fixed point, hashed to SHA-256, SHA-512 and a uint256."
